GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_re_rgb_probe.py:430:#  building the mutant in the form the source permits is what turned a prediction into a measurement.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_re_rgb_probe.py:432:#  THE SOURCE is tiled and the DESTINATION stays LIN_A, deliberately: the RGB arm under test is the
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_re_rgb_probe.py:433:#  GET, and the GET's `linear' comes from src_mode.  A tiled DESTINATION would exercise the PUT and
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_re_rgb_probe.py:434:#  leave this mutant untouched.
