The drawing-engine registers preserve all four colour-type bits, and the line and rectangle callers pass them through unchanged. That supports PUT-default reachability for twelve nibble values. MTE constrains the type separately. I also found a dead MTE branch: `depth` is 8, 16, 32, or 64, but its RGBA selection tests `depth == 4`, so that path always retains CI.
