**Q5: S2’s PUT conclusion survives; its “handled nowhere” inference does not.** Enumerating `mode & 0xf0` gives:

| Masked values | PUT handling |
|---|---|
| `0x00` | CI |
| `0x10` | RGB |
| `0x20` | RGBA |
| `0x30` | ABGR |
| `0x40, 0x50, 0x60, 0x70, 0x80, 0x90, 0xa0, 0xb0, 0xc0, 0xd0, 0xe0` | Default; eleven unnamed values |
| `0xf0` | Default; named YCRCB |

That is **sixteen values, four explicit PUT cases, twelve default values**.

The DE register handler stores the mode without filtering the type nibble. Both line and rectangle callers pass destination mode unchanged. Supported addressing and valid mapping remain prerequisites, but those checks do not constrain the colour nibble. MTE constructs modes separately and is a constrained caller. [Register storage](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1001), [mode loading](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:700), [rectangle PUT](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:928).

